<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Pakao</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1880 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Mandinka district of the middle Casamance known as a centre of Muslim scholarship in a largely non-Muslim region.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Known mainly from oral tradition and colonial records. Pakao was settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandinka">Mandinka</a> families along the north bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casamance">Casamance</a> river, probably by the 16th century, at the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu Empire's</a> sphere.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Pakao was organised as a set of villages under chiefs, but stood out for its clerical lineages, who ran Quranic schools and spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> among neighbouring peoples. It paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu</a> and maintained ties with Gambian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandinka">Mandinka</a> states.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the second half of the 19th century Pakao was caught up in the wars of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fula</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandinka">Mandinka</a> Muslim leaders and then came under French rule, becoming part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-senegal">French Senegal</a> by the 1880s.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1500 CE – 1880 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:7.56%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1880 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mandinka</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Senegal</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pakau, Pakao kingdom</dd></dl></aside></div>

